Z||000000||gomobile||11-02-2001||03:18 PM||||I am thinking of installing a keyless entry for my GT. BUT, before I do I need to confirm something. I was told I also needed to buy 2 relays for the polarity so that I could control the door locks? Can someone out there please confirm if so (ie; it does have power door locks).||||reg||6
Z||000001||Joe Torma||11-02-2001||04:10 PM||||Yes get 2.  If you need wiring diagrams, let me(us) know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000002||gomobile||11-02-2001||04:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Yes get 2.  If you need wiring diagrams, let me(us) know.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>thanks do me a favor and send me the wiring diagrams. As I am more then sure that I will need them. PS: Do I need to remove the skins from the door?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||Joe Torma||11-02-2001||04:19 PM||||Nope, I tapped into the wires by the dead pedal.  My relays are where the wire are...nicely tucked behind the carpet between the door and dead pedal.  I'll draw them up and post later...unless someone beats me to it.||||reg||3
Z||000004||fiero_nightmare||11-02-2001||05:14 PM||||just dont move the battery up front if you put in the keyless entry system. i knew a guy that had keyless entry on his 89 camaro and the battery went dead.   he had fun trying to get the doors open so he could open the hood  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
Z||000005||U Wanna Race||11-02-2001||07:01 PM||||Fiero_Nightmare, why does it matter if the battery is in the front?  And instead of keyless entry do you mean shaved doors?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Lisa 86 2m4||11-02-2001||08:09 PM||||I put in keyless entry in my coupe with power locks several months back.  For the two doors I did not have to do anything special. I connected the wires up under the dash of the passenger foot well and love it!! however, I have been unable to figure out how to hook the trunk release up. That calls for a relay, but I can't figure out the circuit pattern. But that's only the trunk. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bill Osmer||11-02-2001||09:36 PM||||Lisa -<BR>1st 2 questions: 1) do you have electric trunk relase? 2) Does your keyless have an option for trunk release?<P>If the answers are yes to both, then it's REAL easy to add.<P>LMK if you want help<P><P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000008||edbone||11-02-2001||10:39 PM||||The Fieros need a positive trip to activate the door locks. Depending on the keyless entry you are using will determine if you need relays or not. If your keyless says it has a negative output for dl/ul you would have to use relays to convert over to positve output. If the keyless has option for pos. or neg. you wont need to add relays. Just fallow directions for positve output on the keyless.. Eddie||||reg||7
Z||000009||Lisa 86 2m4||11-02-2001||11:42 PM||||Bill,<BR>Yep to both questions. I even bought a relay and played with it for a while but none of the wire combinations worked for me. The keyless has one wire for the trunk, orange, from the receiver. I was trying to connect it to the trunk release wire up on the bottomside of the steering column, my car has a gray/black, a yellow/black and a black/white wire that all are for the trunk release. The relay I purchased later also has 3 wires, one to the reciever and only two to the release. so, now it's sitting in my toolbox taking up room.<P>hey, if you're good with wires....any idea how i could splice my driving lights into my headlight control so they turn on and off with the headlights instead of the switch that came with them?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanx!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||11-03-2001||02:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by edbone:<BR><B>If your keyless says it has a negative output for dl/ul you would have to use relays to convert over to positve output. If the keyless has option for pos. or neg. you wont need to add relays</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Be careful with that!  Check the amp rating of the door control curcuit!  If it is in milliamps you'll fry the curcuit.  I'd use external relays even if you have internal ones(since they are easier to replace!)<P>If you need specific numbers on the relay or wire colors(just probe and test-not difficult) for connections, let me know.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/door.gif"> <P>For the trunk, use the same curcuit, but only 1 relay.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||SLYGUY||11-03-2001||12:58 PM||||I have keyless entry on my GT. It came as an available option with the alarm that the installer hooked up. The remote has two buttons on it. The larger one for enable/disable alarm and lock/unlock the doors, and the smaller second one trips the electric hatch release.<P>As well as being guarded (along with a Club) when I leave the car unattended, it is a great convenience to unlock the doors. Some of our taller PFF members will relate to the low low reach to the key hole in the driver/passenger door to lock/unlock.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfixit58||11-03-2001||08:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Lisa 86 2m4:<BR><B>I put in keyless entry in my coupe with power locks several months back.  ... however, I have been unable to figure out how to hook the trunk release up. That calls for a relay, but I can't figure out the circuit pattern. But that's only the trunk. Hope this helps.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Lisa,<P>The trunk is activated by a relay that's mounted behind the dash, above the steering column on the right. If memory serves, there is a black wire with a white stripe. I think I tapped into it because it's the power feed to the relay. I can talk to you in more detail at this month's meeting.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000013||Lisa 86 2m4||11-04-2001||04:01 PM||||Thanks Roy!<BR>I'll have the relay with me and you can show me what color goes to what. And hopefully, bu meeting time, I'll have both of my new Mr. Mike's seats in!! Finished the passenger one today.....sweeeettttt!!!||||reg||1
